alues":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/100991","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100991","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100991.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100991.patch","merged_at":"2025-01-03T00:08:28Z"},"body":"- Supersedes/closes https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/93653\r\n- Fixes https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/80249\r\n- Fixes https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/57457\r\n- Fixes https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/53793\r\n\r\nHave it calculate the perpendicular vectors by the cross product of the constants vector3 `(1, 0, 0)` or `(0, 1, 0)` depends on the nearest axis and implement the similar[^1] approach as #93653 in a more simple way. Also, for `looking_at()` and `look_at()`, allow this with a warning (and explain it in the document).\r\n\r\n[^1]: This PR may cause a breaking compatibility in that the quaternion of the 180 degree rotation will be inverted for consistency in the direction of rotation, but this is almost never a problem unless you use slerp, etc. in the special situation of generating a 180 degree arc. If you really want to migrate/make compatibility it, the user can align the phase of the quaternion, as in `Quaternion(Basis(Quaternion(v0, v1)))`.","closed_by":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aki